course: dictionary
lesson: 6091
title: Methane, a gas that warms the planet
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Methane is a gas. You cannot see it or smell it, and it burns easily. It is the main part of natural gas, the gas used for cooking and heating. Gases are hard to picture, so use the words around methane to learn what it does.
explain: «Food rotting in a landfill gives off methane, a gas that warms the planet.» The second half of the sentence is the clue: methane warms the planet. The first half tells you where it comes from. Read the whole sentence, not just the hard word.
explain: In science, methane is a greenhouse gas: it traps heat around the Earth. «Cows burp methane, a strong warming gas» shows the same idea. Cows, rice fields, swamps and rubbish tips all give it off. Its formula is CH4, which means one carbon atom and four hydrogen atoms.
fact: Methane is a gas with no colour or smell that burns easily.
fact: Methane is the main part of natural gas, which is used for cooking and heating.
fact: Methane is a greenhouse gas: it traps heat around the planet.
fact: The formula of methane is CH4: one carbon atom and four hydrogen atoms.
fact: Cows, rice fields, swamps and rubbish tips give off methane, and some landfills collect it to make electricity.
exercise: «Food rotting in a landfill gives off methane, a gas that warms the planet.» What is methane? | A solid metal used to make cans | A liquid that cools the air | A type of rubbish bin | *A gas with no colour or smell that burns easily
exercise: «Cows burp methane, a strong warming gas.» Which of these also gives off methane? | Ice cubes in a freezer | Dry sand in a desert | *Rice fields | Clear mountain streams
exercise: Methane is the main part of natural gas. What is natural gas used for? | Building roads | Making paper | *Cooking and heating | Growing flowers
test: Why is methane called a greenhouse gas? | It makes plants grow in glass houses | It is as cold as ice | It turns into a solid when it gets warm | *It traps heat around the planet
test: What does the formula CH4 tell you about methane? | It has no atoms at all | It is a metal made of carbon | It has four carbon atoms and one hydrogen atom | *It has one carbon atom and four hydrogen atoms
exam: «In landfill, rubbish rots without air and bacteria make methane, a gas that warms the planet; some landfills collect it to make electricity.» What is one way landfills use methane? | Burning it to make rain | Storing it as ice in the rubbish | *Collecting it to make electricity | Turning it into solid rock
